  "body": "Looking at rel=\"prev\" and rel=\"next\" I am see [they are not allowed in the body](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/links.html#body-ok).\r\n\r\nWhy is this?\r\n\r\nClickable pagination links are extremely common, especially for 'client-side routing' like image carousels. \r\nWhy can't we use rel attributes \"prev\" and \"next\" on them? Is there an explanation for this constraint anywhere?",
